# The headers the host sends with every answer (Cloudflare Pages reads this file; release 0.2,
# step 17). The page is cross-origin isolated, as the Zemp Specification, section 10, asks:
# only such a page is given the shared memory through which a run is cancelled. The preview
# server of the build reads its headers from this same file, so the tests run under the
# host's own.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# The built files are named by what they hold, so they never change under their name.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
